people.bio:
In his personal life, Ari reads, dances, and raises nerd children outside Boston. In his professional life, he is a computer scientist focusing on socio-technical aspects of software engineering. He has published on a range of topics, including technology adoption, cyberwar, and automated debugging, He does the AI.<br />
<br />
He has a long-standing interest in the history of science and technology. He has a book in production for young people about &quot;what do scientists really do, (why) does it work, and how did it get that way&quot;
